.render/*
node_modules/

# ...except the renderer itself, which is SOURCE, not build output. It has to
# live inside .render/ because Node resolves bare imports (playwright-core,
# ffmpeg-static) by walking up from the importing file, and the only
# node_modules is the one in here -- move it up a level and it stops resolving.
# Ignoring the directory outright (`.render/`) made negation impossible, so the
# rule ignores its CONTENTS and re-includes this one file. Everything else in
# here -- node_modules, frames, the cached audio -- stays ignored.
!.render/render.mjs

# The 58s launch film master is a build output of render-film.mjs (~13MB) and
# is regenerated, so it stays out of git. This rule used to be a blanket
# `*.mp4`, which also swallowed the ad cuts under "ads content/video" -- and
# swallowed them SILENTLY, because a `git add` of an ignored path is a no-op
# rather than an error. Those cuts are deliverables and are tracked.
budgetify-launch-film*.mp4
